[ceiling] These two front rail bearings retain the frame against vertical lift in front-top's sliding receivers. Each square bearing continues the production hooked profile and opens toward the outer flank and rear Y entrance for support removal before assembly. Tree(auto)/Default supports remain the starting treatment for these functional flats; current slice placement, release effort and finished fit require their own scoped review. The native front-rail insertion and installed clearances are recorded in integration-review/rail-motion-check.json.
alternatives: A sloping bearing would cam the frame upward under lift instead of retaining it on a square face. Thickening the rail into its mating channel would consume the defined running clearance. A rear rail pair would occupy back-top's upper screw blocks; the frame uses its front pair and retains the full rear web beside those blocks.
